{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792612147,"nonce":"QaJk4cbA1lxWt497VQ90JIg+8n8=","title":"Report initialization failures against project configuration","message":"An initialization macro failure is currently appended to every opened source file at line 1. In RayDE, UiFramework.register reports undefined Extensions on the package declaration of unrelated files. Its build script supplies local hlwgpu and hlwindow class paths, while build.hxml omits them; the LSP correctly cannot resolve those undeclared sources.\n\nAlign RayDE's editor HXML with the existing native build paths. Keep initialization failures visible against their macro call in the project configuration, rather than inventing a source-code error on every document. Preserve project/import diagnostic contributions in portable editor indexes, restore them through the normal diagnostic aggregation, and clear them when their last contributing document closes.\n\nThe old native binary stops reporting undefined Extensions after correcting the HXML alone, independently of the typing changes. A protocol test covers configuration positioning, unaffected source documents, server restart reuse and diagnostic cleanup. Broader macro compatibility remains separate work.","files":null}]}